      "writtenOn": "2025-05-09T07:02:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I asked Gemini what kind of problematic links this can create:\n\n1. Code Constructs and Technical Identifiers\nobject.property/access_level\n\n2. Version Numbers and Numerical Sequences\nrelease-1.2.3/notes\n\n3.Abbreviations, Citations, and Common Writing Patterns:\nThe regex allows for short domain components, including single letters (due to \\w). This can cause common abbreviations or references to be linkified.\n\nFig. a/b http://Fig.a/b\n\n4. File System Paths or Local Resource Identifiers\nIf a filename or a segment of a path contains a dot and is followed by a slash, it might be captured.\nconfig.v2/settings.xml\n\n5. Ambiguity with Non-HTTP \"Domains\"\ninternal_host.some_department/resource_file \n\n\nI don\u0027t see this as blocker, more just FYI that we can get complains about these.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 136,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 136,
        "endChar": 59
      },
